## Third-Party Runtime Notice (Upstream Slint)

While the slint-d source code and D bindings are MIT-licensed, compiling and linking
with the native Slint runtime configuration (e.g., via libslint_d_bridge) links against
upstream Slint (i-slint-core / slint-interpreter) developed by SixtyFPS GmbH.
Upstream Slint is available under multiple license options:
- GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0-only)
- Slint Royalty-Free Desktop Operating System License (LicenseRef-Slint-Royalty-free-2.0)
- Slint Commercial License (LicenseRef-Slint-Software-3.0)

See https://slint.dev/legal for upstream Slint licensing terms and requirements.
